500 experience'. Under 220 characters. Include 3-5 keywords buyers search."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How long should the LinkedIn About Us be for real estate developer or broker?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"1,200-2,600 characters is the sweet spot (LinkedIn's About Us limit is 2,600 characters). Shorter than 800 chars — under-invested, misses keyword + storytelling opportunity. Longer than 2,600 — truncated by LinkedIn (only first 300-400 chars visible before 'see more' click). Structure: opening hook in first 200 chars (visible without 'see more' click) is CRITICAL. First 3 lines determine whether readers click 'see more' to read the rest."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What are the first 200 characters of the About Us for real estate developer or broker?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"First 200 chars = your elevator pitch. Must include: (1) your role + firm/company, (2) your specific expertise/practice, (3) the buyer/audience you serve, (4) an intriguing hook that makes readers click 'see more'. Example: 'MD, [Firm] | I help Real Estate Developers + Brokers scale beyond 1 senior developer or broker retained on LinkedIn drives Rs 10-100 crore in project-attributed leasing + investment inflow via LinkedIn + Sales Nav. 15 years across [expertise areas]. Recently: [1-line result]. Below: how I work + who I work with.' Test your opening in LinkedIn mobile view (where 70-80% of profile visitors read from) — first 3 lines are what shows."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Should we include contact info in the LinkedIn About Us?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes — critical for lead-gen. Include in P5 (CTA paragraph): email, WhatsApp number, Calendly booking link. For Real Estate Developers + Brokers, add: 'Book a 30-min consultation: [Calendly link]. WhatsApp/email me at [details]. Best for [buyer-type] evaluations of [specific practice].' Also update LinkedIn's 'Contact Info' section separately (accessed via 'Contact info' button on profile). Include: LinkedIn URL, personal website, calendar link, phone (optional), WhatsApp business number."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What are common LinkedIn About Us mistakes for Real Estate Developers + Brokers?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"(1) Copy-pasted corporate bio (impersonal, generic). (2) Third-person voice (unnatural). LinkedIn About Us should be first-person. (3) Buzzword salad ('passionate about', 'thought leader', 'transformative') — reads as fluff. (4) No specific numbers or results. (5) No CTA — where should buyers go next? (6) Ignoring keyword optimization (missing search opportunities). (7) Too long or too short. (8) RERA advertising code + no guaranteed-return promises + investment claims disclosure + confidentiality on tenant deals violations. (9) DIY writing that sounds robotic. (10) Never updated (stale for years)."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How often should we update the LinkedIn About Us?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Quarterly review, annual rewrite. Trigger events: new role, new firm, major client win, new credential, new practice area, book/podcast launch, industry-body appointment, speaking engagement series. For Developer, MD/CEO of real estate firm, Commercial Property Broker (CBRE/JLL/Colliers-tier), REIT founder, Real Estate Fund Manager, the About Us should feel current + reflect your most recent 12-18 months of work. ITD's Growth + Premium tiers include quarterly About Us review + annual rewrite as part of ongoing service."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Should we use emojis in the LinkedIn About Us?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Sparingly + strategically. 2-4 emojis maximum for Real Estate Developers + Brokers — placed as bullet-point substitutes or paragraph-openers to break up text. Use industry-appropriate emojis (📈 for finance, 🏗️ for real estate, 🏭 for manufacturing, 💼 for professional services, 🚀 for tech). Avoid: 🎉🔥💯 (unprofessional for senior Developer, MD/CEO of real estate firm, Commercial Property Broker (CBRE/JLL/Colliers-tier), REIT founder, Real Estate Fund Manager). Test on mobile — some emojis render poorly."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do we need different headlines for LinkedIn versus other platforms?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes — LinkedIn headline is different from Twitter bio or business card. LinkedIn optimizes for: (1) search keywords, (2) buyer-intent language, (3) credential display. Twitter/Instagram optimize for: personality + tone + tagline. Website/business card optimize for: role + firm + contact. For Real Estate Developers + Brokers, LinkedIn headline should be more credential + expertise + keyword-heavy; other channels can be more personality-forward."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How do we make the LinkedIn Featured section work harder?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Featured section = your 3-6 highest-conversion pieces of content pinned above the fold. For Developer, MD/CEO of real estate firm, Commercial Property Broker (CBRE/JLL/Colliers-tier), REIT founder, Real Estate Fund Manager: (1) Top-performing LinkedIn article (choose 1 with 5K+ views if you have one). (2) 1-2 external articles you published (Economic Times, Mint, Business Today, industry publication). (3) 1 case study or long-form thought-leadership piece. (4) 1 speaking engagement or podcast appearance (with link/video). (5) 1 CTA — your Calendly, newsletter subscribe, or lead magnet. Rotate quarterly. Featured section is second most-viewed profile element after About Us."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What tools help write better LinkedIn About Us + headlines?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"For Developer, MD/CEO of real estate firm, Commercial Property Broker (CBRE/JLL/Colliers-tier), REIT founder, Real Estate Fund Manager: (1) Google Docs voice-typing — capture your natural voice, then edit for structure. (2) Grammarly Premium — catch tone + clarity issues. (3) Hemingway Editor — reduce sentence complexity. (4) LinkedIn's own Search — check which keywords your buyers search for. (5) Competitor benchmarking — read 5-10 peer Developer, MD/CEO of real estate firm, Commercial Property Broker (CBRE/JLL/Colliers-tier), REIT founder, Real Estate Fund Manager About Us sections + note patterns. Or outsource entirely to ITD via voice-capture — faster + industry-native + iterated based on performance data."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Where can we see examples of great LinkedIn profiles for Real Estate Developers + Brokers?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Search LinkedIn for senior Developer, MD/CEO of real estate firm, Commercial Property Broker (CBRE/JLL/Colliers-tier), REIT founder, Real Estate Fund Manager + review their profiles. Also study public LinkedIn newsletter authors in your industry — their About Us + headlines are typically well-optimized. For Real Estate Developers + Brokers: search '[your industry] [your role] India OR Dubai OR UK'. Bookmark 8-12 profiles you admire, note their patterns (headline formula, About Us structure, Featured section curation, banner design). ITD's onboarding includes competitive benchmarking against 3-5 peer Developer, MD/CEO of real estate firm, Commercial Property Broker (CBRE/JLL/Colliers-tier), REIT founder, Real Estate Fund Manager in your city + industry."}}]}</script>
