    <div class="itdgl-faq-list" itemscope itemtype="https://schema.org/FAQPage">
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">What is a great LinkedIn About Us template for Real Estate Developers + Brokers?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">Template: 5-paragraph structure. <strong>P1 (Hook):</strong> 'I'm [name], a [role] focused on [specific expertise area] for [buyer type] in [geography/segment].' <strong>P2 (Credibility):</strong> '[X] years in [industry] | [Notable clients/employers or credentials] | [Specific quantified achievement].' <strong>P3 (What you do):</strong> 'My work centers on [3-5 specific practice areas]. Recent examples: [1-2 anonymized case examples].' <strong>P4 (Values + style):</strong> 'My approach: [3-4 principles]. What I'm known for: [distinctive point].' <strong>P5 (CTA):</strong> 'The best way to reach me: [DM / WhatsApp / Calendly link]. Feel free to reach out about [topics]. For [buyer-type] evaluations, book a call [Calendly link].' For Developer, MD/CEO of real estate firm, Commercial Property Broker (CBRE/JLL/Colliers-tier), REIT founder, Real Estate Fund Manager, personalise via voice-capture.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">What LinkedIn headline formulas work best for real estate developer or broker?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">5 headline formulas: (1) <strong>Role + Firm + Expertise + Credential</strong>: 'MD at [Firm] | Wealth Advisory for HNI + Family Offices | CFA, MBA (Wharton)' — best for senior banking/consulting. (2) <strong>What I do + For whom + Result</strong>: 'Helping mid-market manufacturing MDs scale exports 3-5x via LinkedIn + Sales Navigator | Ex-Deloitte' — best for advisory. (3) <strong>Role + Specific outcome</strong>: 'Founder & CEO, [Company] | Building India's largest [category] platform | Rs 400 Cr ARR' — best for SaaS/tech founders. (4) <strong>Credibility + Practice + Speaking-adjacent</strong>: 'Partner @ [Firm] | Real Estate + Commercial Property | 15+ years | Speaker at CREDAI/NAREDCO'. (5) <strong>Advisor + Domain + Approach</strong>: 'Independent Director & Board Advisor | Governance + Strategy + Digital Transformation | Fortune 500 experience'. Under 220 characters. Include 3-5 keywords buyers search.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">How long should the LinkedIn About Us be for real estate developer or broker?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">1,200-2,600 characters is the sweet spot (LinkedIn's About Us limit is 2,600 characters). Shorter than 800 chars — under-invested, misses keyword + storytelling opportunity. Longer than 2,600 — truncated by LinkedIn (only first 300-400 chars visible before 'see more' click). Structure: opening hook in first 200 chars (visible without 'see more' click) is CRITICAL. First 3 lines determine whether readers click 'see more' to read the rest.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">What are the first 200 characters of the About Us for real estate developer or broker?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">First 200 chars = your elevator pitch. Must include: (1) your role + firm/company, (2) your specific expertise/practice, (3) the buyer/audience you serve, (4) an intriguing hook that makes readers click 'see more'. Example: 'MD, [Firm] | I help Real Estate Developers + Brokers scale beyond 1 senior developer or broker retained on LinkedIn drives Rs 10-100 crore in project-attributed leasing + investment inflow via LinkedIn + Sales Nav. 15 years across [expertise areas]. Recently: [1-line result]. Below: how I work + who I work with.' Test your opening in LinkedIn mobile view (where 70-80% of profile visitors read from) — first 3 lines are what shows.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">Should we include contact info in the LinkedIn About Us?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">Yes — critical for lead-gen. Include in P5 (CTA paragraph): email, WhatsApp number, Calendly booking link. For Real Estate Developers + Brokers, add: 'Book a 30-min consultation: [Calendly link]. WhatsApp/email me at [details]. Best for [buyer-type] evaluations of [specific practice].' Also update LinkedIn's 'Contact Info' section separately (accessed via 'Contact info' button on profile). Include: LinkedIn URL, personal website, calendar link, phone (optional), WhatsApp business number.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">What are common LinkedIn About Us mistakes for Real Estate Developers + Brokers?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">(1) Copy-pasted corporate bio (impersonal, generic). (2) Third-person voice (unnatural). LinkedIn About Us should be first-person. (3) Buzzword salad ('passionate about', 'thought leader', 'transformative') — reads as fluff. (4) No specific numbers or results. (5) No CTA — where should buyers go next? (6) Ignoring keyword optimization (missing search opportunities). (7) Too long or too short. (8) RERA advertising code + no guaranteed-return promises + investment claims disclosure + confidentiality on tenant deals violations. (9) DIY writing that sounds robotic. (10) Never updated (stale for years).</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">How often should we update the LinkedIn About Us?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">Quarterly review, annual rewrite. Trigger events: new role, new firm, major client win, new credential, new practice area, book/podcast launch, industry-body appointment, speaking engagement series. For Developer, MD/CEO of real estate firm, Commercial Property Broker (CBRE/JLL/Colliers-tier), REIT founder, Real Estate Fund Manager, the About Us should feel current + reflect your most recent 12-18 months of work. ITD's Growth + Premium tiers include quarterly About Us review + annual rewrite as part of ongoing service.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">Should we use emojis in the LinkedIn About Us?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">Sparingly + strategically. 2-4 emojis maximum for Real Estate Developers + Brokers — placed as bullet-point substitutes or paragraph-openers to break up text. Use industry-appropriate emojis (📈 for finance, 🏗️ for real estate, 🏭 for manufacturing, 💼 for professional services, 🚀 for tech). Avoid: 🎉🔥💯 (unprofessional for senior Developer, MD/CEO of real estate firm, Commercial Property Broker (CBRE/JLL/Colliers-tier), REIT founder, Real Estate Fund Manager). Test on mobile — some emojis render poorly.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">Do we need different headlines for LinkedIn versus other platforms?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">Yes — LinkedIn headline is different from Twitter bio or business card. LinkedIn optimizes for: (1) search keywords, (2) buyer-intent language, (3) credential display. Twitter/Instagram optimize for: personality + tone + tagline. Website/business card optimize for: role + firm + contact. For Real Estate Developers + Brokers, LinkedIn headline should be more credential + expertise + keyword-heavy; other channels can be more personality-forward.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">How do we make the LinkedIn Featured section work harder?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">Featured section = your 3-6 highest-conversion pieces of content pinned above the fold. For Developer, MD/CEO of real estate firm, Commercial Property Broker (CBRE/JLL/Colliers-tier), REIT founder, Real Estate Fund Manager: (1) Top-performing LinkedIn article (choose 1 with 5K+ views if you have one). (2) 1-2 external articles you published (Economic Times, Mint, Business Today, industry publication). (3) 1 case study or long-form thought-leadership piece. (4) 1 speaking engagement or podcast appearance (with link/video). (5) 1 CTA — your Calendly, newsletter subscribe, or lead magnet. Rotate quarterly. Featured section is second most-viewed profile element after About Us.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">What tools help write better LinkedIn About Us + headlines?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">For Developer, MD/CEO of real estate firm, Commercial Property Broker (CBRE/JLL/Colliers-tier), REIT founder, Real Estate Fund Manager: (1) Google Docs voice-typing — capture your natural voice, then edit for structure. (2) Grammarly Premium — catch tone + clarity issues. (3) Hemingway Editor — reduce sentence complexity. (4) LinkedIn's own Search — check which keywords your buyers search for. (5) Competitor benchmarking — read 5-10 peer Developer, MD/CEO of real estate firm, Commercial Property Broker (CBRE/JLL/Colliers-tier), REIT founder, Real Estate Fund Manager About Us sections + note patterns. Or outsource entirely to ITD via voice-capture — faster + industry-native + iterated based on performance data.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">Where can we see examples of great LinkedIn profiles for Real Estate Developers + Brokers?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">Search LinkedIn for senior Developer, MD/CEO of real estate firm, Commercial Property Broker (CBRE/JLL/Colliers-tier), REIT founder, Real Estate Fund Manager + review their profiles. Also study public LinkedIn newsletter authors in your industry — their About Us + headlines are typically well-optimized. For Real Estate Developers + Brokers: search '[your industry] [your role] India OR Dubai OR UK'. Bookmark 8-12 profiles you admire, note their patterns (headline formula, About Us structure, Featured section curation, banner design). ITD's onboarding includes competitive benchmarking against 3-5 peer Developer, MD/CEO of real estate firm, Commercial Property Broker (CBRE/JLL/Colliers-tier), REIT founder, Real Estate Fund Manager in your city + industry.</div>
      </div>
